### Python Coding Conventions

- Use explicit, descriptive names. Avoid 1–2 letter identifiers.
- Prefer guard clauses and early returns; keep nesting shallow.
- Do not swallow exceptions; include actionable messages.
- Keep comments minimal; explain "why" for non-obvious logic.
- Match existing formatting in files; avoid unrelated reformatting.
- Type hints for public APIs and class methods where practical.
- Avoid creating global state; prefer instance attributes.
- For async usage, prefer sync wrappers like `*_sync` where UI requires synchronous calls.
- When editing, ensure no linter errors are introduced.
